Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [configuration]

Enable ssh-env shell integration feature by default in Ghostty.
When operating across mixed Linux environments (e.g. SSHing to Ubuntu or
Fedora hosts), remote hosts lack Ghostty's terminfo entry for TERM=xterm-ghostty,
causing curses applications such as htop and top to fail.
Defaulting ssh-env to true automatically propagates TERM=xterm-256color and
preserves truecolor capabilities via COLORTERM without requiring manual
per-user config changes. Users can override with `shell-integration-features = no-ssh-env`.
Fixes: projectbluefin/dakota#1800

--- a/src/config/Config.zig
+++ b/src/config/Config.zig
@@ -8610,7 +8610,7 @@ pub const ShellIntegrationFeatures = packed struct {
     cursor: bool = true,
     sudo: bool = false,
     title: bool = true,
-    @"ssh-env": bool = false,
+    @"ssh-env": bool = true,
     @"ssh-terminfo": bool = false,
     path: bool = true,
 };
